  "question": {
    "text": "<span style=\"font-size:11.0pt\"><span style='font-family:\"Georgia\",serif'>Consider the function </span></span><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mfrac></msup></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math>,where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>]</mo></math> denotes the greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> denotes the set of all ordered pairs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo> </mo></math>is continuous at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, then the number of elements in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is :",
